{"name":"Hindu Lotus","hex":"#ee4d83","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lotus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of the genus Nelumbo of aquatic plants in the family Nelumbonaceae.","A water lily (Nymphaea), especially those of Egypt or India. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lotus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nelumbo nucifera","blocks":[{"text":"Nelumbo nucifera, also known as Padma or Kamala, sacred lotus, pink lotus, Indian lotus, or simply lotus, is one of two extant species of aquatic plant in the family Nelumbonaceae. It is sometimes colloquially called water lily, though this more often refers to members of the family Nymphaeaceae. The lotus belongs in the order Proteales."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Sacred_lotus_Nelumbo_nucifera.jpg/330px-Sacred_lotus_Nelumbo_nucifera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nelumbo_nucifera","wikidata":"Q16528"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Sacred_lotus_Nelumbo_nucifera.jpg/500px-Sacred_lotus_Nelumbo_nucifera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Sacred_lotus_Nelumbo_nucifera.jpg/1280px-Sacred_lotus_Nelumbo_nucifera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Sacred_lotus_Nelumbo_nucifera.jpg/500px-Sacred_lotus_Nelumbo_nucifera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASacred_lotus_Nelumbo_nucifera.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Lotus_field.jpg/120px-Lotus_field.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https: